# CODEOWNERS
# This file defines who is automatically requested for review when a
# pull request touches certain paths. For a single-maintainer
# personal fork, the maintainer (@yuri-schmaltz) owns everything.
# Listing the critical paths explicitly is a defensive measure:
# any future branch-protection rule that requires a CODEOWNER
# approval will use this list to determine which paths are
# "protected".

# Default owner for everything
*   @yuri-schmaltz

# Critical paths: workflows, packaging, build config, security.
# These are listed separately to make it easy to add a stricter
# branch-protection rule later (e.g. require approval on changes
# to release pipelines).
/.github/workflows/    @yuri-schmaltz
/.github/dependabot.yml @yuri-schmaltz
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @yuri-schmaltz
/.github/SECURITY.md    @yuri-schmaltz
/debian/                @yuri-schmaltz
/pires-forge.spec       @yuri-schmaltz
/pyproject.toml         @yuri-schmaltz
/pixi.toml              @yuri-schmaltz
/MANIFEST.in            @yuri-schmaltz
/scripts/               @yuri-schmaltz
